# Copy to .env and fill in what you need:   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and edited by a human only -- the edit guard refuses an
# agent's write to it, and .claude/settings.json denies reading it. This file is
# committed, so it holds placeholders and never a real key.
#
# Every variable the project reads is listed here. tests/conftest.py's
# clean_env fixture sets each of them empty before a test runs, so a test can never
# pass or fail depending on whose machine it runs on. Add a variable here first.
#
# Read by src/starter/config/settings.py; the process environment wins over
# this file, and the file never enters the environment.
#
# LangSmith is never used (docs/decisions/0004-langgraph-runs-locally.md): no
# LangSmith key and no tracing switch belong here. scripts/serve.sh refuses to
# start a server while .env sets one.

# -- The model: your local Open WebUI (connect-openwebui-model) ---------------
# All three, or none -- none keeps the offline model; some is refused, naming
# what is missing. Open WebUI must have API keys switched on (admin setting
# ENABLE_API_KEYS) and your user the "API Keys" permission.
#
# OPENWEBUI_URL=http://localhost:3000     # the address you open in a browser (or its /api)
# OPENWEBUI_API_KEY=sk-...                # Settings > Account > API Keys
# OPENWEBUI_MODEL=llama3.1:8b             # the model id exactly as Open WebUI lists it
#
# The model must have no tools, filters or web search attached inside Open
# WebUI: those run there, outside the assistant's allow-lists and budgets.

# -- The task list (task-store-read-only) ------------------------------------
# A SQLite file; `uv run starter tasks add "title"` adds to it. Empty means
# .data/tasks.sqlite3 in this repository; a relative path is taken from here.
#
# TASKS_DB=.data/tasks.sqlite3
